---
// src/components/blog/visuals/ExecutiveFunctionVisual.astro
---

<div class="apple-glass-card apple-specular-top my-10 p-5 sm:p-7 rounded-3xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm bg-gradient-to-br from-white/95 via-gray-50/50 to-amber-50/20 text-left">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-4">
    <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500"></span>
    <h3 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-lg sm:text-xl tracking-tight m-0">
      The ADHD Dopamine Bridge: Overcoming Morning &amp; Homework Inertia
    </h3>
  </div>

  <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    ADHD is not an inability to focus—it is a chemical dysregulation of task initiation (Russell Barkley, Ph.D.). Here is why verbal shouting fails and how a physiological dopamine bridge restores momentum:
  </p>

  <div class="space-y-4">
    <!-- Step 1: The Wall -->
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center gap-4 bg-white/90 border border-gray-100 p-4 rounded-2xl">
      <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-red-100 text-red-900 font-extrabold flex items-center justify-center text-sm shrink-0">
        1
      </div>
      <div class="flex-grow">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm mb-0.5">The Executive "Wall of Awful"</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed m-0">
          The ADHD brain experiences zero natural dopamine for low-stimulation tasks (waking up, packing a backpack, opening a math worksheet). They feel literal cognitive paralysis.
        </p>
      </div>
      <span class="text-xs text-red-700 bg-red-50 border border-red-200 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full font-bold shrink-0">
        Dopamine Deficit
      </span>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 2: The Trap -->
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center gap-4 bg-white/90 border border-gray-100 p-4 rounded-2xl">
      <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-amber-100 text-amber-900 font-extrabold flex items-center justify-center text-sm shrink-0">
        2
      </div>
      <div class="flex-grow">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm mb-0.5">The Common Trap: Shouting &amp; Threats</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed m-0">
          Parents raise their voices to create adrenaline. While adrenaline <em>can</em> force movement, it burns out the nervous system and creates morning fight-or-flight trauma.
        </p>
      </div>
      <span class="text-xs text-amber-700 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full font-bold shrink-0">
        Adrenaline Spike
      </span>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 3: The Clinical Bridge -->
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center gap-4 bg-emerald-50/80 border border-emerald-200 p-4 rounded-2xl">
      <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 text-white font-extrabold flex items-center justify-center text-sm shrink-0 shadow-xs">
        3
      </div>
      <div class="flex-grow">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-emerald-950 text-sm mb-0.5">The Clinical Solution: The 5-Minute Dopamine Bridge</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-emerald-900 leading-relaxed m-0">
          Pair the difficult start with warm sensory input: upbeat music, an energetic snack, co-working ("body doubling"), or breaking task #1 into an absurdly easy 30-second chunk.
        </p>
      </div>
      <span class="text-xs text-emerald-800 bg-emerald-100 border border-emerald-300 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full font-bold shrink-0">
        Neuro-Affirming
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
